// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects child processes spawned by DbgSrv.exe, a Microsoft debugging process server that can be
//   abused to execute arbitrary processes through a trusted developer utility.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of DbgSrv.exe to create processes during debugging sessions
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/58c62744ab84ad3049c09ba2c613f0e744d92c9c/yml/OtherMSBinaries/Dbgsrv.yml
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/debugger/dbgsrv-command-line-options
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ef3b3d4c0282e589c70b2f35e2adcf5aff966e6f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dbgsrv_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dbgsrv.exe"
